// Test: bugfixes/sem007_sibling_call_in_stateless_class
// Grammar: class_body → functions_block → method calling sibling method
// Regression: SEM007 (fingerprint 32e3513b6c13...)
// Bug:  When a stateless utility class (no parent, no fields, body doesn't
//       reference `this`) has one method call another sibling method, the
//       typechecker auto-marks both methods as `is_static`. The sibling
//       call site was emitted as a MethodCall that pushed `this` as the
//       receiver, but the callee had no `this` parameter — the receiver
//       leaked onto the operand stack. The bug surfaced as "this used in
//       method without instance parameter" via the cross-file `shared:`
//       manifest path; standalone it produced a silent stack imbalance
//       caught downstream (CODEGEN-INVALID-WASM). Both share a root cause
//       — see commit c9e3b55c (mir: skip pushing receiver for is_static
//       utility-class methods).
// Expected output:
//   hi

start:
	A x = A()
	print(x.outer())

class A
	functions:
		string inner()
			return "hi"
		public:
			string outer()
				return inner()
